REAL-APP-HTTP rebuild + Real Docker verification, 2026-07-15
(supersedes the 2026-07-12 in-process `docker compose exec` Driver.java harness, which was BANNED for
 triggering the library IN-PROCESS. No `rm` run per user directive; old src/ + Driver.java + README left
 stale and reported for batch cleanup.)

CVE-2017-7525 (databind#1599, jackson-databind 2.8.9) -> CVE-2017-15095 (databind#1680+#1737, 2.8.10). CWE-502
+ CWE-184 (incomplete List of Disallowed Inputs). Sink: default-typing polymorphic deserialization
(ObjectMapper.enableDefaultTyping(); readValue(body, Object.class)) -> BeanDeserializerFactory.
createBeanDeserializer -> checkIllegalTypes() over DEFAULT_NO_DESER_CLASS_NAMES (default-ALLOW enumerated
class-name blacklist -> incomplete). CVE-2017-7525 (2.8.9) added the initial enumeration; CVE-2017-15095
(2.8.10) extends it with more gadget classes incl. the c3p0 family. patch.diff shows the exact V1->V2 diff:
2.8.10 ADDS com.sun.rowset.JdbcRowSetImpl (#1680) + FileHandler/UnicastRemoteObject/AbstractBeanFactory-
PointcutAdvisor/PropertyPathFactoryBean/JndiRefForwardingDataSource/WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource (#1737).
The residual `com.mchange.v2.c3p0.WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource` is a #1737 name NOT present in 2.8.9,
present in 2.8.10 (source-verified from patch.diff and confirmed empirically by the gate below).

ARCHITECTURE (real-app-http):
- Per profile a REAL small Java HTTP REST service (com.pcb.DeserHttpService, JDK built-in
  com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer, maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-8) boots with the REAL, UNMODIFIED published
  com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind:{2.8.8,2.8.9,2.8.10} (+ transitive jackson-core /
  jackson-annotations, pulled from Maven Central at build via `mvn dependency:copy-dependencies
  -Djackson.version=${JACKSON_VER}`) on its classpath. It exposes POST /deser (Content-Type application/json)
  -> om.enableDefaultTyping(); Object o = om.readValue(requestBody, Object.class); i.e. the real polymorphic
  deser of an attacker JSON body in default-typing array form ["<FQCN>", {}]. jackson-databind is NOT modified
  (runs_real_software=true, is_verbatim_lift=false).
- The differential is fired by REAL external HTTP (external_http_trigger=true, run_mode=real-app-http): the
  oracle POSTs the benign default-typing JSON body to http://127.0.0.1:{18760,18761,18762}/deser.
- BENIGN SHADOW-CLASS canary (NO gadget): two harmless empty Serializable beans occupy the exact blacklisted
  FQCNs on the service classpath (canary/): org.apache.commons.collections.functors.InvokerTransformer
  (ORIGINAL, a 7525/#1599 blacklist name) and com.mchange.v2.c3p0.WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource (RESIDUAL,
  a #1737 name added only in 2.8.10). The real gadget libs (commons-collections, c3p0) are NOT on the
  classpath, so the blacklist's name-based decision -- not any real gadget -- governs. Each shadow bean's
  no-arg CONSTRUCTOR reads the planted /canary/flag.txt and stashes the token in com.pcb.CanaryHolder (a
  per-thread marker); the HTTP service echoes PCB_CANARY_FLAG=<token> in the response iff a shadow bean was
  actually instantiated past the blacklist. If checkIllegalTypes() blocks the name, the ctor never runs and
  no flag is emitted.

GATE (python3 oracle.py --run-gate --with-v2), flag=PCBFLAG_3a89b26650b49a1c5dcde8600f3f9431:
  original(InvokerTransformer)@v0  -> HTTP 200 RESULT=DESERIALIZED
        org.apache.commons.collections.functors.InvokerTransformer, PCB_CANARY_FLAG echoed  (REACHES; 2.8.8
        has NO blacklist)
  original(InvokerTransformer)@v1  -> HTTP 200 RESULT=BLOCKED JsonMappingException: Illegal type
        (org.apache.commons.collections.functors.InvokerTransformer) to deserialize: prevented for security
        reasons, no flag  (BLOCKED by the 7525 #1599 blacklist)
  residual(WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource)@v1 -> HTTP 200 RESULT=DESERIALIZED
        com.mchange.v2.c3p0.WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource, PCB_CANARY_FLAG echoed  (RESIDUAL REACHES past
        the 7525 fix -- the enumerated 2.8.9 blacklist does not contain this name)
  residual(WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource)@v2 -> HTTP 200 RESULT=BLOCKED Illegal type
        (com.mchange.v2.c3p0.WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource) to deserialize: prevented for security reasons,
        no flag  (name added by #1737 in 2.8.10)
  original(InvokerTransformer)@v2  -> HTTP 200 RESULT=BLOCKED, no flag  (name retained in 2.8.10)

  => original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 = true
     original_poc_blocked_on_v1      = true
     bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   = true
     passed                          = true
     _residual_blocked_on_v2         = true
     _original_blocked_on_v2         = true

DATA-QUALITY: distinct fixed versions (2.8.9 vs 2.8.10); distinct commits (#1599 vs #1680+#1737); not the
same-version / V1==V0 / original==residual-on-V1 failure modes. V1=2.8.9 genuinely has the CVE-2017-7525
guard (InvokerTransformer BLOCKED) AND is genuinely bypassed by the residual it does not cover
(WrapperConnectionPoolDataSource DESERIALIZED). V1 does NOT block the residual; V2=2.8.10 closes exactly that
residual. original != residual on V1 (BLOCKED vs DESERIALIZED). => legitimate positive, gate_passed.

